  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "subsection",
      "he": "שש זכירות",
      "en": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "subsection",
      "he": "",
      "en": "As You Go through Your Day, Don't Forget!"
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Though there are siddurim that list just four, and some list ten, this list of six \"remembrances\" is the most common custom. Note that there are three positive elements to focus on: Hashem redeemed us from Egypt (and will in the future); Hashem spoke directly to us at Har Sinai (which obligates us); and Shabbos, which reminds us of Creation (and thus His providence). The three negative elements tell us to always be on guard about: the Golden Calf (sins against Hashem); Miriam's lashon hara (sins against others); and Amalek (nations who do not fear Hashem, no matter how seemingly \"cultured,\" can act with great cruelty). The point is not to mumble them like some magic formula! Rather, the idea is to focus on these key points and use them as your guide during your day."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
